U('choose-a-tool',2,'选工具：功能更多就更合适吗','比较文章',[
 ['When comparing two writing tools, it is tempting to count features and choose the one with the longer list. That approach is easy to explain, but it can hide the tasks that matter most. A tool with advanced layout controls may be a poor choice for someone who mainly needs to write short messages on several devices. Another tool may look simpler but handle search, export and offline editing more predictably. A useful comparison starts with the work, not with the size of the feature list.','比较两个写作工具时，人们容易数功能，选择清单更长的那个。这种方法容易解释，却可能掩盖真正重要的任务。拥有高级排版功能的工具，未必适合主要在多设备上写短消息的人。另一工具看起来更简单，却可能在搜索、导出和离线编辑上更可预期。有效比较应从工作出发，而不是从功能清单长度出发。'],
 ['For a small trial, choose a few realistic tasks and perform them in both tools. Write a note, find it later, move it to another device and export a copy that can be opened elsewhere. Record where you need extra steps or lose information. A polished demonstration prepared by the seller can show what is possible, but it may not reveal the friction in your own routine. Do not treat a task as successful merely because the first screen looks correct.','小规模试用时，选择几个真实任务，在两个工具中都执行：写笔记、之后找回、移到另一设备、导出能在别处打开的副本。记录哪些环节需要额外步骤或丢失信息。卖家准备的精美演示能展示可能性，却未必揭示你日常流程中的阻碍。不要只因为首屏看起来正确就认为任务成功。'],
 ['Costs include more than the subscription price. Consider the time needed to move existing material, explain the tool to collaborators and recover when a preferred feature is unavailable. Also check how easily you can leave. An export button is useful only if the exported result preserves the parts you need and can be used in another environment. These questions do not imply that a complex tool is always worse. They make the trade-offs explicit instead of hiding them behind popularity or appearance.','成本不只是订阅价，还包括迁移旧资料、向协作者解释工具，以及常用功能不可用时恢复工作的时间。也应检查能否容易离开：导出按钮只有在导出结果保留必要内容、能在其他环境使用时才有意义。这不代表复杂工具总更差，而是要明确权衡，不能用流行程度和外观掩盖。'],
 ['The final choice may reasonably differ between people. Someone who prepares long publications may value controls that another person never uses. Write down the reasons for your choice and the conditions that would make you reconsider it. Then stop comparing for a while and use the tool for real work. A comparison is meant to support a decision, not become an endless activity that replaces the work the tool was supposed to help with.','不同人作出不同选择完全合理。编写长出版物的人可能看重另一个人从不用的功能。记录选择理由和需要重新考虑的条件，然后暂停比较，使用工具完成实际工作。比较旨在支持决策，不该成为取代实际工作的无止境活动。']
],[['feature list','功能清单','Start with tasks rather than the feature list.'],['realistic task','实际场景中的任务','Compare tools using realistic tasks.'],['friction','阻碍；额外操作负担','The trial revealed friction in the export process.'],['trade-off','取舍；权衡','Make the trade-offs explicit.'],['reconsider','重新考虑','State when you would reconsider the choice.']],[[
 '作者建议如何开始工具比较？',['先明确重要任务','只数功能数量','直接选演示最漂亮的'],0,'第一段的 starts with the work 明确了出发点。'],['为什么导出按钮本身还不够？',['要验证导出内容是否保留所需信息并能使用','按钮必须是绿色','导出永远没价值'],0,'第三段限制了导出功能真正有用的条件。'],['最终选择不同是否说明必有一人错误？',['一定','不一定，任务与需求可能不同','只有最流行的工具才正确'],1,'最后一段解释不同工作可有不同合理选择。']
],{task:'比较两种虚构工具，为你的英文读写练习作出选择。',audience:'想了解你选择理由的朋友',length:'180～250 词',requirements:['用具体任务而非功能数比较','讨论迁移、导出或协作成本','说明决定及重新考虑的条件'],starter:'My main tasks are…\nIn the trial,…\nI would reconsider if…',model:'My main tasks are reading short documents, keeping useful expressions and writing messages that I can revise later. I compared two fictional tools by completing those tasks rather than counting their features.\n\nTool A offers advanced layouts and many templates. Tool B is simpler, but I could find an old note quickly and export the original and revised drafts together. In both tools, I wrote a short message, searched for it and opened an exported copy elsewhere. Tool A required more steps to preserve the revision history.\n\nFor now, I would choose Tool B. The export process fits my routine, and I do not need the layout controls often enough to justify moving all my material. This does not mean Tool A is worse for everyone. Someone preparing long publications might value its features much more.\n\nI would reconsider if I began writing documents that require complex formatting, or if Tool B stopped preserving the information I need in exports. I will keep a backup and use the chosen tool for several weeks before comparing again. The purpose of this decision is to support regular reading and writing, not to spend all my study time choosing software.'});
U('practice-routine',2,'学习计划：用完成任务代替打卡数字','学习随笔',[
 ['A person can maintain a long study streak without becoming much better at the tasks they care about. Opening an application every day is easy to count, while understanding a difficult sentence or writing a clear request is harder to measure. The count may still be useful as a reminder, but it should not become the entire definition of progress. If the goal is written communication, the routine needs regular opportunities to understand and produce meaningful text.','一个人可以连续打卡很久，却未必更擅长自己关心的任务。每天打开应用容易统计，理解难句或写清请求却难以衡量。数字仍可作为提醒，但不应成为进步的全部定义。如果目标是书面沟通，日常练习就要经常提供理解和写出有意义文本的机会。'],
 ['A manageable session might begin with one short passage. Read it before opening the translation, then write a brief explanation of its main point. Check one uncertain condition or reference, not every word you already understand. Next, write a message connected to the topic. For example, after reading instructions about changing a reservation, ask for a new time and confirm what will happen to the original booking. This makes the language serve a purpose rather than remain a list of isolated facts.','一次可完成的练习可以从短文开始。先读，再打开译文，写出主旨的简短说明。核对一个不确定的条件或指代，而不是逐一检查已经理解的词。接着写与主题有关的消息，例如读过改约说明后，请求新时间并确认原预约如何处理。这让语言服务于目的，不再只是孤立事实的清单。'],
 ['Feedback is most useful when it leads to another attempt. Keep the first draft, note the important corrections and write a revised version yourself. Later, try a similar task without looking at the model. If the same problem appears again, record it as something to practise rather than treating one correction as permanent mastery. You do not need to collect every possible error in a large notebook; a small set of recurring problems is often easier to review meaningfully.','反馈在促成再次尝试时最有用。保留初稿，记下重要修改，自己写修改版。之后不看范文做相似任务。如果同一问题再次出现，将它记作待练项目，而不是把改过一次当成永久掌握。不必在大笔记本中收集所有可能错误，一小组反复出现的问题往往更容易有效复习。'],
 ['The routine should also survive ordinary busy days. A shorter version could be one paragraph and one reply, while a longer session could include a complete article and a second draft. Missing a day does not erase previous work. What matters is returning to tasks that reveal whether you can understand more accurately and express yourself with less help. The plan should make that return easy, instead of turning every interruption into a reason to abandon it.','练习也应能适应普通的忙碌日。短版可以是一段阅读加一条回复，长版则包括全文和二稿。少学一天不会抹去以往成果，重要的是回到能检验理解是否更准确、表达是否更少依赖帮助的任务。计划应让回归容易，而不是让每次中断都成为放弃理由。']
],[['study streak','连续学习记录','A long study streak is not the only sign of progress.'],['manageable','可以应付的；适量的','Choose a manageable session.'],['isolated facts','孤立事实','Language is more than isolated facts.'],['another attempt','另一次尝试','Useful feedback leads to another attempt.'],['recurring problem','反复出现的问题','Review a small set of recurring problems.']],[[
 '作者认为打卡数字完全无用吗？',['完全无用','不是，可作提醒但不能代表全部进步','数字等于完整语言能力'],1,'第一段承认提醒价值并限制结论。'],['为什么在阅读后安排相关写作？',['让语言用于具体目的','为了避免理解文章','为了只复制范文'],0,'第二段通过改约例子说明目的性。'],['收到修改建议后最重要的后续是什么？',['只收藏漂亮答案','自己再尝试，并在新任务中检验','立即把所有旧稿删掉'],1,'第三段将反馈与再次尝试连接起来。']
],{task:'写一份适合自己的读写练习安排。',audience:'未来一周的自己',length:'180～240 词',requirements:['设定具体阅读和写作任务','安排反馈后的修改及相似任务复测','为忙碌日提供缩短版本，并说明进步依据'],starter:'My regular session will…\nAfter feedback,…\nOn a busy day,…',model:'My regular session will begin with one passage about a task I might actually encounter, such as installing software or changing an appointment. I will read it independently and write down the main point before opening the reference translation. Then I will check any condition, negative statement or reference that I misunderstood.\n\nI will write a short English message related to the passage. I will keep the original draft and use feedback to identify problems that affect the meaning. After reviewing the reasons, I will write the revised version myself. A few days later, I will try a similar task without looking at the model to see whether I can use the correction independently.\n\nOn a busy day, I will shorten the session to one paragraph and one useful reply. Missing a session will not require restarting the whole plan. I will simply return to the next manageable task.\n\nI will judge progress by whether I can understand similar instructions more accurately and write complete requests with less help. A streak may remind me to practise, but it will not replace those observations. I will review a small number of recurring problems each week rather than collect every correction without using it.'});
U('reading-a-chart',2,'图表上升了，结论就成立吗','数据解读',[
 ['A team introduces a new help page and later reports that support requests fell by twenty percent. The change looks promising, but the chart alone does not explain why it happened. Perhaps the page helped users solve common problems. Perhaps fewer people used the product during that period, or a separate software update removed the problem that had generated many requests. Several explanations can fit the same downward line. The report should make clear what was observed and what is being inferred.','团队新增帮助页后，报告支持请求减少了百分之二十。变化看似可喜，但图表本身无法解释原因。可能是文章帮助用户解决问题，也可能那段时间使用者更少，或另一软件更新消除了曾导致大量求助的问题。同一条下降曲线可以符合多种解释，报告应区分观察与推断。'],
 ['Start with the denominator. A fall from one hundred requests to eighty means something different if active users fell by half. It also matters whether “requests” counts messages, separate problems or people contacting support. One unresolved case may generate several messages. If the counting rule changed between the two periods, the comparison may reflect the measurement method rather than a real improvement in user experience. Numbers need definitions as well as labels.','先看分母。如果活跃用户减少一半，请求从一百降到八十就有不同含义。还要知道请求统计的是消息数、独立问题数，还是联系支持的人数。一个未解决案例可能产生多条消息。如果两段时间计数规则改变，对比反映的可能是测量方法，而不是真实体验改善。数字既需要标签，也需要定义。'],
 ['Next, examine the comparison period and other changes. A short holiday week may not be comparable with a normal working week. The team could look at requests per active user, separate the topics covered by the page and review whether users actually found the article useful. None of these checks guarantees a perfect causal answer, but together they can make the interpretation more credible. It is better to describe partial evidence accurately than to make a confident claim that ignores obvious alternatives.','接着检查对比时段与其他变化。短暂假期周不一定能与正常工作周比较。团队可以查看每位活跃用户的请求、分开统计帮助页涉及的主题，并检查用户是否真的认为文章有用。这些检查不能保证完美因果结论，但能共同提升解释的可信度。准确描述部分证据，比自信地忽略明显替代解释更好。'],
 ['A careful summary might say that requests declined after publication and that the result is consistent with the page being useful, while noting the other changes and the limited observation period. It would avoid saying that the page “proved” a twenty-percent reduction. This distinction is useful when reading product announcements, workplace dashboards or news articles. Ask what the number measures, what it is compared with and how far the evidence supports the explanation.','谨慎的总结可以说，发布后请求下降，结果与文章有效的解释相符，同时注明其他变化和观察时间限制。应避免声称文章“证明”带来了百分之二十下降。阅读产品公告、工作仪表盘或新闻时也可这样做：问数字测量什么、与什么相比，以及证据支持解释到何种程度。']
],[['denominator','分母','Check the denominator before comparing totals.'],['counting rule','计数规则','The counting rule must remain consistent.'],['causal explanation','因果解释','The chart does not establish a causal explanation.'],['consistent with','与……相符','The result is consistent with the page helping users.'],['observation period','观察时段','The observation period was short.']],[[
 '支持请求下降是否单独证明帮助页导致改善？',['证明','不证明，还存在其他解释','证明所有用户已读文章'],1,'第一段列出多个可以产生同一变化的因素。'],['为什么要关注活跃用户数？',['它影响总请求数的解释','用户数永远与请求无关','只为让图表更复杂'],0,'第二段用请求数和用户数同时变化的例子解释分母。'],['什么表述更符合文中证据？',['文章被证明精确降低百分之二十求助','发布后请求下降，但原因仍有限制和替代解释','请求下降代表所有问题已解决'],1,'最后一段给出有分寸的总结。']
],{task:'为“新帮助页让求助减少 20%”写一份谨慎的数据评论。',audience:'阅读团队周报的人',length:'180～250 词',requirements:['区分观察和因果结论','列出需要核对的分母、计数规则及其他变化','给出准确而有用的替代表述'],starter:'The observed change is…\nBefore attributing it to…\nA more careful summary would be…',model:'The observed change is that recorded support requests fell from one hundred to eighty after the new help page was published. That is a twenty-percent fall in the count, but it does not by itself establish that the page caused the change.\n\nBefore attributing it to the article, we should check how many people were actively using the product in each period. We also need to confirm whether the count refers to messages, separate problems or individual users. If one case produces several replies, a change in the counting rule could affect the result.\n\nOther developments may matter. A software update might have removed a common problem, and a holiday week might have reduced activity. We could examine requests per active user, focus on topics covered by the article and collect feedback from readers. These checks would improve the evidence without guaranteeing a perfect causal explanation.\n\nA more careful summary would be: support requests declined after publication, and the result is consistent with the article helping some users. However, the observation period is short and other changes may have contributed. We should continue checking those factors before making a stronger claim.'});
U('open-source-request',2,'向开源项目提需求：表达需要，而非下命令','社区沟通',[
 ['A feature request is more useful when it explains a problem than when it only names a preferred solution. “Add automatic export” leaves maintainers to guess what work the requester is trying to complete. A stronger request might explain that a team needs a readable copy of its notes outside the application at the end of each week. That context allows people to consider several approaches, including ones the requester has not thought of.','功能请求解释问题时，比只报出偏好方案更有用。“添加自动导出”会让维护者猜用户想完成什么工作。更有力的请求可以说明，团队每周结束时需要一份能在应用之外阅读的笔记副本。背景信息使大家能考虑多个方案，包括请求者尚未想到的方案。'],
 ['Before opening a new issue, read the project’s contribution guidance and search for related discussions. If a similar request exists, add the missing use case rather than repeating the title. Describe the environment and constraints that matter: whether the process must work offline, whether formatting needs to survive and whether another tool already handles part of the task. Avoid including private documents merely to make the example realistic. A small sample can often demonstrate the requirement without exposing real material.','新建议题前，请阅读贡献指南并搜索相关讨论。如果已有相似请求，补充缺失的使用案例，而不是重复标题。描述相关环境与限制：是否需离线、是否保留格式、是否已有工具处理部分任务。不必为让例子真实而加入私人文档，小样例往往足以表达需求而不暴露真实资料。'],
 ['A request is not a delivery agreement. Maintainers may have limited time, and the proposed feature may conflict with the project’s purpose or create a long-term support burden. Asking whether the idea fits the project is more productive than presenting a deadline that nobody accepted. You can offer to test a prototype, improve documentation or help clarify the design. Such offers should be specific and realistic rather than implying that a quick patch will remove every maintenance cost.','请求不是交付协议。维护者时间可能有限，功能也可能偏离项目目标或增加长期支持负担。询问想法是否适合项目，比给出无人接受的截止日期更有建设性。你可以提出测试原型、改进文档或澄清设计，但承诺应具体、现实，不能暗示小补丁能消除所有维护成本。'],
 ['If the answer is no, it is reasonable to ask which requirement does not fit or whether an external extension would be appropriate. It is also reasonable for the project to leave the feature out. Good written communication does not guarantee agreement. It gives the people involved enough information to make a clear decision while keeping the discussion focused on the task and the project’s constraints.','如果被拒绝，可以合理询问哪个需求不适合，或外部扩展是否合适。项目不纳入该功能也可能合理。良好书面沟通不保证达成一致，而是提供足够信息，让各方明确决策，并将讨论集中在任务及项目限制上。']
],[['feature request','功能请求','A feature request should explain the problem.'],['use case','使用案例','Add the missing use case.'],['support burden','支持负担','The feature may create a support burden.'],['fit the project','符合项目方向','Does this idea fit the project?'],['prototype','原型','I can help test a prototype.']],[[
 '强功能请求首先应解释什么？',['要解决的实际问题','维护者必须何时交付','请求者拥有多少设备'],0,'第一段将任务背景与仅报方案相对照。'],['已有相似议题时，更有用的做法是什么？',['重复同标题要求立刻做','补充未覆盖的使用案例','公开私人文档'],1,'第二段建议补充信息而不是重复。'],['沟通清楚是否能保证功能被接受？',['保证','不能，项目仍有范围和维护限制','拒绝就说明没人看懂'],1,'末段直接区分有效沟通与必然同意。']
],{task:'给一个虚构开源笔记项目写功能请求。',audience:'项目维护者',length:'180～250 词',requirements:['从问题和使用场景出发','交代已查讨论、约束和小样例','询问项目契合度，提出具体帮助，不强加期限'],starter:'Problem and use case:\nCurrent workaround:\nWould this fit…?',model:'I would like to ask whether scheduled export fits the direction of this notes project. Our small team needs a readable copy of its shared notes outside the application at the end of each week. At present, one person exports the notes manually and checks that the headings and links are preserved.\n\nI searched the existing discussions and found a request about exporting individual notes, but it did not cover repeated export of a selected collection. Our process needs to work without a permanent network connection. Plain text with headings and links would be sufficient; we do not need every layout detail. I can provide a small sample collection without private information.\n\nOne possible solution is a scheduled export feature, although an external extension might be more appropriate. Could you advise whether either approach matches the project’s scope? I understand that this request is not a delivery agreement and that ongoing maintenance matters.\n\nI can test a prototype against our sample collection and help document the expected output. If the feature does not fit the project, guidance on a supported external workflow would still be useful. There is no deadline attached to this request.'});
U('remote-work-proposal',2,'工作制度讨论：别把偏好当结论','议论文章',[
 ['Discussions about remote work often begin with a universal claim: people are always more productive at home, or collaboration only happens in an office. Both statements compress many different tasks into one conclusion. Writing a report, training a new colleague and repairing physical equipment do not place the same demands on a team. A useful proposal should identify which work it is trying to improve instead of assuming that one location is best for every purpose.','讨论远程工作时，常以普遍断言开头：在家总更高效，或只有办公室才能协作。这两种说法都将许多不同任务压缩为同一个结论。写报告、培训新人、维修实体设备对团队的要求不同。有效提案应指出想改善哪类工作，而不是假定一个地点适合所有目的。'],
 ['For a small documentation team, fewer interruptions may help people complete long drafts. At the same time, a new member may need quick explanations that experienced colleagues no longer notice they are providing. A proposal that measures only the number of finished pages could miss the cost of slower onboarding or unclear decisions. Likewise, counting time spent online may reward visible activity without showing whether the documentation became more useful. The measure needs to reflect the work, not just what is easy to count.','对小型文档团队而言，减少打断可能帮助完成长稿。但新人可能需要快速解释，资深同事甚至已察觉不到自己在提供这些帮助。只衡量完成页数可能漏掉入职变慢或决策不清的成本；统计在线时长也可能奖励可见活动，却不能说明文档是否更有用。衡量应反映工作，而不只是容易计数的东西。'],
 ['A limited trial could combine protected writing periods with scheduled opportunities for questions and review. The team should agree on how urgent issues are raised, where decisions are recorded and which tasks require shared availability. It should also ask participants whether the arrangement creates uneven costs. A person with a quiet workspace may experience the trial differently from someone sharing a small room. An average result can hide those differences if nobody looks for them.','有限试用可以结合不被打断的写作时段与固定答疑、审查时间。团队应约定紧急问题如何提出、决定在哪里记录，以及哪些任务需要共同在线。也应询问安排是否带来不均等成本。拥有安静工作空间的人与共享小房间的人，体验可能不同；若不主动调查，平均结果会掩盖差异。'],
 ['Before the trial begins, state what would count as a reason to continue, change or stop it. Review work quality, response delays and the experience of newer colleagues as well as output. The outcome might support a mixed arrangement rather than a simple victory for one side. A good proposal does not need to settle the future of work for everyone. It needs to justify a workable decision for this team under clearly stated conditions.','试用前说明什么结果足以支持继续、修改或停止。除了产出，也检查质量、答复延迟和新人的体验。结果可能支持混合安排，而不是某一方简单胜出。好的提案不必解决所有人的工作未来，只需在明确条件下，为这个团队论证可行决策。']
],[['universal claim','普遍性断言','Avoid a universal claim based on one task.'],['interruption','打断','Long drafts require fewer interruptions.'],['onboarding','入职引导','The trial should not make onboarding harder.'],['uneven costs','不均等的成本','Ask whether the policy creates uneven costs.'],['workable decision','可行的决定','The proposal supports a workable decision.']],[[
 '作者为何反对单凭“在家总更高效”作决定？',['不同任务与人员条件不同','因为所有远程工作都失败','因为办公室永远不需要沟通'],0,'首段列举不同任务，质疑普遍结论。'],['只统计完成页数可能遗漏什么？',['新人培养和决策沟通成本','页面数量本身','文件名长度'],0,'第二段指出衡量范围不足。'],['试用结果必须让某种制度全面获胜吗？',['必须','不必，可能支持混合安排','只许统计在线时间'],1,'最后一段强调为特定团队作有条件决策。']
],{task:'为文档团队设计一个工作安排试用方案。',audience:'团队负责人',length:'180～250 词',requirements:['明确任务需求及不同成员情况','写清专注时段、沟通和记录规则','定义继续或调整的观察标准'],starter:'For this team, the main problem is…\nI propose a limited trial…\nWe will review…',model:'For this team, the main problem is that frequent interruptions make long drafts difficult to finish. However, new colleagues also need timely help, so a plan focused only on uninterrupted writing would be incomplete. I propose a four-week trial rather than a permanent rule for every task.\n\nDuring the trial, we will protect two writing periods each week and schedule separate times for questions and review. Urgent problems should use the agreed support channel, while ordinary decisions should be recorded in the project notes. Work involving a new colleague may require shared availability even during an otherwise flexible week.\n\nWe will review the quality of completed articles, response delays and the experience of newer team members. Page counts and online time will not be treated as complete measures of success. We should also ask whether people have suitable workspaces and whether the arrangement creates uneven costs.\n\nIf writing improves without making help difficult to obtain, we can continue the arrangement. If onboarding slows or urgent issues remain unanswered, we should revise the schedule. The result may support a mixed approach. The purpose is to find a workable arrangement for this team, not prove that one location is always best.'});
U('respectful-disagreement',2,'不同意，也能把讨论往前推','观点与沟通',[
 ['A clear disagreement does not have to begin with a judgment about the other person. In a project discussion, “This makes no sense” tells the reader that something is wrong but gives little help in deciding what to change. A more useful reply identifies the part you disagree with and the consequence you are concerned about. It may also state what you accept, so the discussion does not restart from a false impression that every part of the proposal is rejected.','明确反对不必先评价对方。在项目讨论中，“这毫无道理”只告诉读者有问题，却很少帮助决定该改什么。更有用的回复指出反对哪部分、担心什么后果，也可说明接受的部分，避免让讨论基于“整份提案都被否定”的错误印象重新开始。'],
 ['Suppose a team proposes removing the manual export button because automatic synchronisation is now available. You might agree that automatic synchronisation reduces routine work while disagreeing that it replaces export. A user may still need a separate copy that remains available after an account is closed or a mistaken deletion is synchronised. Explaining that scenario gives the team something concrete to assess. It is stronger than saying that users will “obviously hate” the change without evidence.','例如团队因已有自动同步，提议移除手动导出。你可以赞同同步减少日常工作，却反对它能替代导出。用户可能仍需一份独立副本，以便账户关闭或误删已同步后仍可用。解释这个场景能让团队具体评估，比没有证据地说“用户显然会讨厌”更有力。'],
 ['The reply should separate established facts from assumptions. If support records show repeated requests for independent copies, cite that evidence without claiming that it represents every user. If you are describing a possible risk, call it a risk and suggest how to check it. You can propose a smaller change, such as making export less prominent while keeping it available, or ask which requirement would justify removing it completely. This turns disagreement into a choice among explicit options.','回复应区分已知事实与假设。如果支持记录显示多次有人要求独立副本，可以引用，但不要声称代表所有用户。如果描述的是潜在风险，就称其为风险，并建议如何检查。可以提出更小改动，例如降低导出入口显眼程度但仍保留，或询问什么需求足以支持彻底删除。这让分歧成为明确选项间的选择。'],
 ['Politeness is not the same as hiding your position. A message can say “I do not support removing export in this release” and still be respectful if it explains the reason and engages with the goal. Excessive softening can make the decision unclear, while aggressive language can move attention from the issue to the relationship. The practical aim is to make your position, evidence and proposed next step easy to understand, even if the final decision goes another way.','礼貌不等于隐藏立场。只要解释理由并回应目标，“我不支持本次发布移除导出”也可以尊重他人。过度缓和会让决定不清，攻击性语言则把注意力从问题移到关系。实际目标是让立场、证据和下一步易懂，即使最终决定并不与你一致。']
],[['disagree with','不同意','I disagree with removing the export option.'],['false impression','错误印象','Avoid the false impression that everything is rejected.'],['independent copy','独立副本','Some users need an independent copy.'],['established fact','已确认的事实','Separate established facts from assumptions.'],['engage with','认真回应；处理','Engage with the goal of reducing complexity.']],[[
 '赞同自动同步，是否必须赞同删除导出？',['必须','不必，两者解决的问题可能不同','同步能替代任何独立备份'],1,'第二段用同意一部分、反对另一部分说明区别。'],['提出潜在风险时，应如何表达？',['当作已经发生的普遍事实','说明是风险并建议验证','编造所有用户都反对'],1,'第三段要求区分事实和假设。'],['礼貌表达是否意味着不能明确说不支持？',['意味着','不意味着，可明确立场并解释理由','必须省略所有理由'],1,'最后一段给出直接而尊重的反对示例。']
],{task:'回复一份“已有云同步，因此删除手动导出”的提案。',audience:'提出方案的同事',length:'180～240 词',requirements:['说明认可的目标与明确反对点','区分已知事实和需要核查的风险','给出折中方案及具体下一步'],starter:'I agree that…\nHowever, I do not support…\nCould we check… before…?',model:'I agree that automatic synchronisation reduces routine work and that the interface should avoid unnecessary controls. However, I do not support removing manual export in this release. Synchronisation and an independent copy serve different purposes.\n\nA user may need a copy that remains available after an account is closed. A synchronised deletion may also reach every connected device, so the presence of synchronisation does not by itself answer that need. These are possible scenarios we should investigate; I am not claiming that every user relies on export or that the proposed change has already caused data loss.\n\nCould we review existing support requests and ask a small group of users how they keep independent copies? That would give us better evidence about the requirement before removing the only visible route to it.\n\nAs a smaller change, we could move export to the file menu while keeping it documented and available. This would reduce prominence without removing the capability immediately. If another supported feature fully meets the same need, I would be willing to reconsider. For now, I suggest keeping export and recording the evidence needed for a later decision.'});
